Exclusive breastfeeding for the first six months means that the infant receives only breast milk without water, honey, ghutti, glucose or formula milk as breast milk alone meets all nutritional and hydration needs during this period and protects the infant against infection. From six months onwards, age-appropriate complementary foods should be introduced while breastfeeding continues up to two years and beyond.

Mothers are also being guided on correct positioning and attachment and encouraged to adopt the feeding position most comfortable for them and their baby. Frequent feeding on demand and support from Anganwadi Workers, ASHA workers or the nearest healthcare facility whenever difficulty is faced are being emphasised through the week. Mothers returning to work are being counselled on expressing and safely storing breast milk so that feeding continues uninterrupted.

मां का दूध-शिशु के लिए सबसे पहला और सबसे उत्तम आहार
सही तरीके और सही पोज़िशन से स्तनपान करना, मां और शिशु दोनों के लिए आरामदायक और लाभकारी होता है
आइए, इस वीडियो में जानें-स्तनपान के सही तरीके और आसान पोज़िशन, ताकि हर फीड बने सुरक्षित, सहज और पोषण से भरपूर
#WorldBreastfeedingWeek

pic.twitter.com/Y7hys038QJ
— Ministry of WCD (@MinistryWCD)
August 5, 2026

The Ministry calls upon healthcare professionals, community workers, families and citizens to create an enabling environment in which every mother is empowered to breastfeed and every child receives the best possible start in life.

Breast milk is a complete food for an infant, providing all the energy and nutrients needed during the first six months of life
